The adaptive sampling pattern's last direction of a ring with an even count

dtObstacleAvoidanceQuery::sampleVelocityAdaptive, for an even adaptiveDivs,
wrote a ring's last direction one slot past the one it then counted
(pat[npat*2+2], pat[npat*2+3] before npat++): the counted slot was never
written, so the crowd sampled an uninitialised direction (a different velocity
by platform, compiler and profile), and with adaptiveDivs 32 and adaptiveRings
4 (both at their limits) the write went past the end of pat (on the stack).
The direction goes to the slot it counts, as upstream issue #496 proposes
(https://github.com/recastnavigation/recastnavigation/issues/496, also #798);
an odd adaptiveDivs (the default is 7) is unchanged. Not yet upstream.

Apply from upstream/recastnavigation, after 0001: git apply -p1 ../../patches/0003-adaptive-pattern-even-divs.patch

diff --git a/DetourCrowd/Source/DetourObstacleAvoidance.cpp b/DetourCrowd/Source/DetourObstacleAvoidance.cpp
index 56bed74..fc23145 100644
--- a/DetourCrowd/Source/DetourObstacleAvoidance.cpp
+++ b/DetourCrowd/Source/DetourObstacleAvoidance.cpp
@@ -571,8 +571,8 @@ int dtObstacleAvoidanceQuery::sampleVelocityAdaptive(const float* pos, const flo
 
 		if ((nd&1) == 0)
 		{
-			pat[npat*2+2] = last2[0]*ca - last2[1]*sa;
-			pat[npat*2+3] = last2[0]*sa + last2[1]*ca;
+			pat[npat*2+0] = last2[0]*ca - last2[1]*sa;
+			pat[npat*2+1] = last2[0]*sa + last2[1]*ca;
 			npat++;
 		}
 	}
